---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/site";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Privacy Policy" }];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="HomeDIYCalc privacy policy: calculator inputs stay in your browser, no analytics or ads, and how emails you send us are handled."
  canonical="/privacy-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: November 23, 2026.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc is a fully static website operated independently by an
      individual based in Malaysia. This policy describes what happens to
      the information involved in using the site: calculator inputs are
      processed in your browser and are not sent anywhere; the site does
      not ask you for personal information; and the only personal
      information the operator receives is what you choose to send by
      email. Our hosting provider processes request data to serve and
      protect the site; see §§4 and 6.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. Data we collect</h2>
    <p>
      The site has no accounts, no registration, no login, and no contact
      form. It does not ask for your name, email address, or any other
      identifying information, and calculator inputs are processed entirely
      in your browser and are never sent to a server (see §2). The only
      personal information the operator receives is what you choose to send
      by email (see §7). Separately, our hosting provider processes
      standard request data, such as IP addresses in server logs, and may
      set security cookies to serve and protect the site (see §§4 and 6).
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Calculator inputs</h2>
    <p>
      Measurements and prices you enter into a calculator are processed entirely in your
      own browser. They are never sent to a server, because there is no server. Closing
      the page discards them.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Saved projects (LocalStorage)</h2>
    <p>
      Items you explicitly choose to save are stored in your browser's LocalStorage, under the key
      <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">homediycalc:project:v1</code>.
      That data stays on your device. It is not transmitted anywhere, not shared with
      anyone, and not accessible to us. Clearing your browser data deletes it. Nothing is
      saved unless you click save.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      The site itself sets no cookies and runs no analytics. There are no
      third-party tracking scripts on the site. Our hosting provider,
      Cloudflare, may set cookies for security purposes (for example to
      protect against bots or abuse) and may process standard web-server
      information as part of serving and protecting the site; see §6.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      No advertising scripts are loaded on this site. Google AdSense is disabled by
      default. If advertising is ever enabled, this policy will be updated first, and the
      change will be recorded in the project's decision log.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">6. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      The site loads no third-party scripts, fonts, or content by default. The pages are
      served as static files from our hosting provider, Cloudflare Pages. The site is
      deployed on Cloudflare Pages: the public production deployment is pending the
      owner's launch approval, and the staging preview is access-restricted (sign-in
      required via Cloudflare Access) and not public. Cloudflare processes requests to
      serve and protect the site and may log standard web-server information, such as
      IP addresses in access logs. How Cloudflare handles that information is governed
      by Cloudflare's own privacy policy. Signing in to the access-restricted staging
      preview involves Cloudflare processing the email address you sign in with, for
      authentication only.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">7. Contacting us</h2>
    <p>
      Our contact email is{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="underline">{SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you write
      in the message. We use that information only to read and answer your
      message. We do not sell, share, or add it to any mailing list, and we
      do not use it for advertising. Do not send sensitive personal
      information by email.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">8. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is intended for adults undertaking home improvement projects. It does not
      ask anyone — adult or child — for personal information, and calculator inputs are
      processed in the browser and are not sent anywhere. The only personal information
      the operator receives is what a person chooses to send by email (see §7).
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes — for example, if advertising or analytics is ever enabled —
      the updated policy will be posted here with a new “last updated” date before the
      change takes effect.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
